Do we need a nil check for the SchedulingQueue? Previously, we only included that check in the snippet below for the sake of the tests.
```golang
	// Update the scheduling queue with the nominated pod information. Without
	// this, there would be a race condition between the next scheduling cycle
	// and the time the scheduler receives a Pod Update for the nominated pod.
	// Here we check for nil only for tests.
	if sched.SchedulingQueue != nil {
		sched.SchedulingQueue.AddNominatedPod(logger, podInfo.PodInfo, nominatingInfo)
	}
```
I don't think we need a nil check for every queue usage. Please remove those and keep only the original one.

