The `supportsFamily:` method on `id<MTLDevice>` was introduced in iOS 13.0. If the application runs on iOS 12 (which is still supported by some versions of Flutter), calling this method directly will cause a crash due to an unrecognized selector. To prevent this, we should guard the call by checking if the device responds to the selector.

```
  if (![layer.device respondsToSelector:@selector(supportsFamily:)] ||
      ![layer.device supportsFamily:MTLGPUFamilyApple3]) {
    return NO;
  }
```

